.TH BIT 1 "August 2026" "bitpkg" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bit \- Bit package manager (bitpkg)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bit
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPACKAGES...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bit
is a lightweight, hybrid source/binary package manager. It supports interactive configuration, dynamic compiler swapping, automatic dependency resolution, and direct binary overlaying.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B h
Show the help menu.
.TP
.B l
List installed packages.
.TP
.B c
Open interactive configuration menu to set PREFIX, data paths, compiler (CC), and default behavior (source vs binary).
.TP
.B s, u
Sync or update the local repository from the configured Git URL.
.TP
.B re
Reinstall or update the package manager itself from the Git repository.
.TP
.B b [-s] \fI<pkgs...>\fR
Build the specified package recipe(s). Use \fB-s\fR to skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
.B bi [-s] \fI<pkgs...>\fR
Build and immediately install the specified package recipe(s).
.TP
.B i [-s] \fI<pkgs...>\fR
Install a package that has already been compiled in the build directory.
.TP
.B r [-s] \fI<pkgs...>\fR
Remove the specified package(s) and clean up leftover build artifacts.
.TP
.B fi [-b] \fI<path>\fR
Install a package from a local file. Pass the path to a source recipe, or use \fB-b\fR to install directly from a binary \fB.tar.xz\fR archive.
.SH REPOSITORY STRUCTURE
The package repository is split into two main sections:
.IP \[bu] 2
\fBmain/\fR: Contains directories for each package, housing the \fBrecipe\fR file.
.IP \[bu] 2
\fBbinary/\fR: Contains directories for each package, housing the pre-compiled \fB.tar.xz\fR archive structured for the target PREFIX.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by apiwo.
